  "body": "Somewhat related to #5548, and will probably also be fixed as part of moving downloads into the navigation algorithm, but this is a separate issue:\r\n\r\nIf you put `<a href=\"https://example.com/\" download>Click me</a>` on a page, this will not download example.com, at least in Chrome and Firefox: http://boom-bath.glitch.me/download-example.html\r\n\r\nThe current spec does not allow this. It allows bailing out and doing nothing, but the \"download a hyperlink\" algorithm never gets to the navigation algorithm.",
